tain organs or glands (twenty in number, supposed to be in the belly), ŚBr. xii, xiii", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "N. of a section of the AV. (xx, 127 and 128 according to Sāy. on AitBr. vi, 32; or xx, 127-136 according to the MSS.), ŚāṅkhBr.; ŚāṅkhŚr.; ĀśvŚr.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "kunti": [{"id": "kunti", "headword": "कुन्ति", "headword_slp1": "kunti", "fold": "kunti", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "कुन्ति m. pl. N. of a people, Kāṭh.; Pāṇ. iv, 1, 176; MBh. &c.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "a prince of that people (also called Kunti-bhoja), Hariv. &c.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "N. of a son of Dharma-netra, VP.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "of a son of Netra and grandson of Dharma, BhP. ix, 23, 21 ff.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "of a son of Kratha, BhP. ix, 24, 3; VP.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "of a son of Vidarbha and father of Dhṛṣṭa, Hariv.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "of a son of Supārśva and grandson of Sampāti and great-grandson of Garuḍa, MārkP.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "of a son of Kṛṣṇa, BhP. x, 61, 13.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["कुंति", "कुंतिः", "कुन्तिः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["kuMti", "kuMtiH", "kuntiH"]}, {"id": "kuntI", "headword": "कुन्ती", "headword_slp1": "kuntI", "fold": "kunti", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "कुन्ती f. N. of Pṛthā (daughter of a Yādava prince named Śūra [or Vasu, Hariv. 5255], who gave her to his childless cousin Kunti or Kuntibhoja, by whom she was adopted;\nshe afterwards became one of the wives of Pāṇḍu;\non one occasion before her marriage she paid such respect to the powerful sage Durvāsas that he taught her an incantation or charm, by virtue of which she was to have a child by any god she liked to invoke;\nout of curiosity she invoked the Sun, by whom she had a child, cf. कर्ण;\nbut the Sun afterwards restored to her her maidenhood;\nsoon after his marriage Pāṇḍu retired to the woods to indulge his passion for hunting;\nthere he killed a male and female deer, who turned out to be a Ṛṣi and his wife in the form of these animals;\nthe sage cursed Pāṇḍu and predicted that he would die in the embrace of one of his wives ;\nhence Pāṇḍu lived apart from Kuntī, but with his approval she made use of her charm and had three sons, Yudhiṣṭhira, Bhīma, and Arjuna, by the three deities Dharma, Vāyu, and Indra respectively;\ncf. माद्री), Pāṇ.;\nMBh. &c.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "N. of a Rākṣasī, Buddh.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "of a river, VP.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "the wife of a Brāhman, L.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "the plant Boswellia thurifera, L.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "a fragrant resin (= गुग्गुलु), L.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "kuntijit": [{"id": "kuntijit", "headword": "कुन्तिजित्", "headword_slp1": "kuntijit", "fold": "kuntijit", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "कुन्ति—जित् m. ‘conqueror of Kuntī’, N. of a prince, VP.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "kuntinandana": [{"id": "kuntinandana", "headword": "कुन्तिनन्दन", "headword_slp1": "kuntinandana", "fold": "kuntinandana", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "कुन्ति—नन्दन for कुन्ती-न्˚, q.v.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}, {"id": "kuntInandana", "headword": "कुन्तीनन्दन", "headword_slp1": "kuntInandana", "fold": "kuntinandana", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "कुन्ती—नन्दन m. either of the three elder Pāṇḍava princes.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "kuntiBoja": [{"id": "kuntiBoja", "headword": "कुन्तिभोज", "headword_slp1": "kuntiBoja", "fold": "kuntiBoja", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "कुन्ति—भोज m. N. of a Yādava prince (king of the Kuntis, who adopted Kuntī), MBh.; Hariv. &c.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "कुन्ति—भोज m. pl. N. of a peo